Keep a password manager's secret copy from a sandbox's window

niri offers no data control on a wp-security-context-v1 socket, but a
window of such a client that has the keyboard is offered the clipboard
and the primary selection through its data device, as any focused
window is. So a secret a password manager copied, marked as one by
x-kde-passwordManagerHint as wl-copy --sensitive does, reached a
sandbox's window whenever it had the focus, or took it while the
secret was held.

So niri records, as each selection is set, whether its types carry a
password manager's mark, as the clipboard door judges one, and offers
that selection to no restricted client while it does: the seat's
selection focus goes to nobody instead. A secret withholds at once,
since smithay calls new_selection before it stores and offers the
selection; any other copy offers again once the store is done, so the
secret it replaces is never handed over. A screenshot niri copies
itself is no secret. Joel's own windows are offered everything as
before. It adds no setting, since a sandbox's connection and the
copy's own types decide it.

